      "evidence": [
        {
          "location": "T:p2-b5",
          "quote": "Han et al. (2025) analyzed the full HVS Survey dataset\n(Brown et al. 2014), which includes 21 unbound late\nB-type main sequence stars with well-measured atmo-\nspheric parameters such as efective temperature, sur-\nface gravity, and projected rotational velocity (v sin i).\nFrom this sample, Han et al. (2025) identified several\nHVSs that likely originated from the LMC. In this study,\nwe focus on HVS 3, HVS 7, and HVS 15—the three\nstars with the highest likelihood of LMC origin, based\non orbits that are incompatible with a Galactic center\nejection."
        },
        {
          "location": "T:p3-b5",
          "quote": "the HVSs are traveling so fast (several times the local escape velocity)"
        }
      ],
      "source": "2510.03393v2"
    }
